{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_number": 1,
      "text": "         Machine learning\n           with scikit-learn\n                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN\n\n\n\n\n\nGeorge Boorman\nCore Curriculum Manager, DataCamp"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 2,
      "text": "What is machine learning?\n\n  Machine learning is the process whereby:\n    Computers are given the ability to learn to make decisions from data\n\n     without being explicitly programmed!\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 3,
      "text": "Examples of machine learning\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 4,
      "text": "Unsupervised learning\n\n  Uncovering hidden patterns from unlabeled data\n\n  Example:\n    Grouping customers into distinct categories (Clustering)\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 5,
      "text": "Supervised learning\n\n  The predicted values are known\n\n  Aim: Predict the target values of unseen data, given the features\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 6,
      "text": "Types of supervised learning\n\n   Classification: Target variable consists of       Regression: Target variable is continuous\n  categories\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 7,
      "text": "Naming conventions\n\n  Feature = predictor variable = independent variable\n\n  Target variable = dependent variable = response variable\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 8,
      "text": "Before you use supervised learning\n\n  Requirements:\n   No missing values\n\n    Data in numeric format\n\n    Data stored in pandas DataFrame or NumPy array\n\n\n\n  Perform Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) first\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 9,
      "text": "scikit-learn syntax\n\n from sklearn.module import Model\n model = Model()\n model.fit(X, y)\n predictions = model.predict(X_new)\n print(predictions)\n\n\n array([0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0])\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 10,
      "text": "    Let's practice!\nSUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 11,
      "text": "         The classification\n              challenge\n                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN\n\n\n\n\n\nGeorge Boorman\nCore Curriculum Manager, DataCamp"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 12,
      "text": "Classifying labels of unseen data\n\n 1. Build a model\n\n2. Model learns from the labeled data we pass to it\n\n3. Pass unlabeled data to the model as input\n\n4. Model predicts the labels of the unseen data\n\n\n\n  Labeled data = training data\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 13,
      "text": "k-Nearest Neighbors\n\n  Predict the label of a data point by\n    Looking at the k closest labeled data points\n\n    Taking a majority vote\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 14,
      "text": "k-Nearest Neighbors\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 15,
      "text": "k-Nearest Neighbors\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 16,
      "text": "k-Nearest Neighbors\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 17,
      "text": "KNN Intuition\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 18,
      "text": "KNN Intuition\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 19,
      "text": "Using scikit-learn to fit a classifier\n\n from sklearn.neighbors import KNeighborsClassifier\n X = churn_df[[\"total_day_charge\", \"total_eve_charge\"]].values\n y = churn_df[\"churn\"].values\n print(X.shape, y.shape)\n\n\n (3333, 2), (3333,)\n\n\n knn = KNeighborsClassifier(n_neighbors=15)\n knn.fit(X, y)\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 20,
      "text": "Predicting on unlabeled data\n\n X_new = np.array([[56.8, 17.5],\n                   [24.4, 24.1],\n                   [50.1, 10.9]])\n print(X_new.shape)\n\n\n (3, 2)\n\n\n predictions = knn.predict(X_new)\n print('Predictions: {}'.format(predictions))\n\n\n Predictions: [1 0 0]\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 21,
      "text": "    Let's practice!\nSUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 22,
      "text": "          Measuring model\n           performance\n                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN\n\n\n\n\n\nGeorge Boorman\nCore Curriculum Manager, DataCamp"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 23,
      "text": "Measuring model performance\n\n   In classification, accuracy is a commonly used metric\n\n  Accuracy:\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 24,
      "text": "Measuring model performance\n\n  How do we measure accuracy?\n\n  Could compute accuracy on the data used to fit the classifier\n\n  NOT indicative of ability to generalize\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 25,
      "text": "Computing accuracy\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 26,
      "text": "Computing accuracy\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 27,
      "text": "Computing accuracy\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 28,
      "text": "Train/test split\n\n from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X, y, test_size=0.3,\n                                                     random_state=21, stratify=y)\n knn = KNeighborsClassifier(n_neighbors=6)\n knn.fit(X_train, y_train)\n print(knn.score(X_test, y_test))\n\n\n 0.8800599700149925\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 29,
      "text": "Model complexity\n\n  Larger k = less complex model = can cause underfitting\n\n  Smaller k = more complex model = can lead to overfitting\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 30,
      "text": "Model complexity and over/underfitting\n\n train_accuracies = {}\n test_accuracies = {}\n neighbors = np.arange(1, 26)\n for neighbor in neighbors:\n     knn = KNeighborsClassifier(n_neighbors=neighbor)\n     knn.fit(X_train, y_train)\n     train_accuracies[neighbor] = knn.score(X_train, y_train)\n     test_accuracies[neighbor] = knn.score(X_test, y_test)\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 31,
      "text": "Plotting our results\n\n plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n plt.title(\"KNN: Varying Number of Neighbors\")\n plt.plot(neighbors, train_accuracies.values(), label=\"Training Accuracy\")\n plt.plot(neighbors, test_accuracies.values(), label=\"Testing Accuracy\")\n plt.legend()\n plt.xlabel(\"Number of Neighbors\")\n plt.ylabel(\"Accuracy\")\n plt.show()\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 32,
      "text": "Model complexity curve\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 33,
      "text": "Model complexity curve\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                  SUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 34,
      "text": "    Let's practice!\nSUPERVISED LEARNING WITH SCIKIT-LEARN"
    }
  ],
